# The raw statewide density exports: 144.6 MB of HTML across seven states. In the
# six ABS-2021 exports most of the bulk is hex ring arrays, which
# apps/trip-density/ derives from the H3 index instead; Victoria uses a different
# generator and ships as-is. Committing these would put 144.6 MB in git history
# permanently, in every clone, even after deletion.
# tools/prepare-trip-density.py reads from here and writes the publishable pages;
# only those are tracked.
assets/state-based-trips-heatmap/

# Build tools live in the working copy (portfolio-rebuild/tools/), not here.
# DEPLOY.md is explicit that tools/ is never published. A copy gets dropped in
# to run against this tree, but it is not site content.
tools/

# Tool output, not site content: per-state figures printed while regenerating the
# maps. Nothing on the site fetches it — the published figures live in
# docs/trip-density-maps.md.
apps/trip-density/_stats.json
